From: Mesa packaging <makepkg@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] nvk: advertise VK_NV_low_latency2

Expose the extension in the device extension table.  The entry points
are implemented in nvk_nv_low_latency2.c and wired up automatically by
vk_entrypoints_gen from the Vulkan API XML once the extension is listed
here.

Note: place this alongside other .NV_* entries so the table stays
grouped by vendor prefix, matching the convention used throughout
nvk_physical_device.c.

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
@@ -1,2 +1,3 @@
       .NV_mesh_shader                               = true,
+      .NV_low_latency2                              = true,
       .NV_shader_sm_builtins                        = true,
